# codex-system-test
# @req REQ-WEB-BROWSER-003 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-004 REQ-WEB-BROWSER-021
"""# CSS Grid auto-size item stretch

**Requirements:** doc/02_requirements/feature/simple_web_browser_engine_production_hardening.md
**Plan:** doc/03_plan/sys_test/grid_auto_item_stretch.md
**Design:** doc/05_design/simple_web_browser_engine_production_hardening.md
**Research:** doc/01_research/domain/simple_web_browser_engine_production_hardening.md

## Overview

This bounded scenario proves that non-replaced Grid items with an automatic
block size stretch across one explicit pixel row when effective self-alignment
is `normal` or `stretch` and neither block-axis margin is automatic.

It covers the canonical production path:

1. authored HTML and CSS;
2. parsed semantic nodes;
3. resolved computed `Style` values;
4. shared layout boxes;
5. canonical `DrawIrComposition` commands;
6. the existing Engine2D software executor;
7. exact framebuffer pixels.

No Grid-specific Draw IR command is introduced.

No private painter or backend path is introduced.

The Web semantic/layout owner remains responsible for used geometry.

Engine2D consumes the resulting canonical composition unchanged.

## Standards contract

CSS Grid item alignment uses the item's `align-self` when it is not `auto`.

Otherwise, the Grid container's `align-items` value is effective.

For the bounded non-replaced items covered here, `normal` behaves as stretch.

Stretch applies only when the authored block size remains automatic.

An authored height therefore remains authoritative.

An automatic top or bottom margin owns block-axis free space and suppresses
stretching.

Physical top and bottom margins are outside the stretched border box.

For `box-sizing:content-box`, physical padding and borders are deducted before
the used CSS height is materialized.

## Syntax

The primary container uses:

```css
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: 4px 4px;
grid-template-rows: 4px;
gap: 0;
align-items: stretch;
```

The children intentionally have backgrounds but no authored height.

The negative controls use:

```css
align-self: start;
margin-top: auto;
height: 2px;
height: 0px;
grid-column: 1 / span 2;
```

The box-model control combines one-pixel top and bottom margins, padding, and
borders inside an eight-pixel explicit row.

The nested control uses `align-items:normal` on its outer Grid and retains an
inner `2px 2px` template after temporary height resolution.

## Examples

The primary fixture is exactly 8 by 4 pixels.

The Grid box is `[0, 0, 8, 4]`.

The red item box is `[0, 0, 4, 4]`.

The blue item box is `[4, 0, 4, 4]`.

Each framebuffer row contains four red pixels and four blue pixels.

All four framebuffer rows are asserted literally.

The expected red command color is `0xFFDC2626`.

The expected blue command color is `0xFF2563EB`.

The expected clip is `[0, 0, 8, 4]`.

The Engine2D skipped-command count is exactly zero.

## Negative controls

The `align-self:start` item remains `[0, 0, 4, 1]`.

The automatic-margin item remains `[4, 0, 4, 1]`.

The explicitly sized item remains `[8, 0, 4, 2]`.

The content-box item becomes `[12, 1, 4, 6]` inside its eight-pixel row.

The authored `height:0px` item remains `[16, 0, 4, 1]`; numeric zero is not
used as a proxy for the `auto` keyword.

The split-cascade item keeps authored `height:0px` and `align-items:stretch`
metadata after an unrelated inline `visibility` declaration forces the full
Style reconstruction path; it remains `[12, 8, 4, 1]`.

Cross-phase final writing modes map authored logical zero sizes onto physical
height consistently: vertical `inline-size:0px` and horizontal
`block-size:0px` both retain `height_px == 0`, `height_auto == false`, and a
one-pixel intrinsic box.

The two-column span remains `[0, 8, 8, 1]` rather than being stretched by the
single-track rule.

The explicitly stretched `video` remains `[8, 8, 4, 1]` because replaced
elements are outside this bounded stretch implementation.

The two-row span remains `[16, 8, 4, 1]` rather than being stretched by the
single-track rule.

These controls prevent a blanket rule that assigns every Grid child the row
height.

## Nested Grid control

The nested Grid is an automatic-height item of a four-pixel outer row.

The outer container uses `align-items:normal`.

The nested Grid stretches to `[0, 0, 4, 4]`.

Its own `grid-template-columns` remains `2px 2px`.

Its own `grid-template-rows` remains `4px`.

Its left child becomes `[0, 0, 2, 4]`.

Its right child becomes `[2, 0, 2, 4]`.

This catches incomplete `Style` clones that discard Grid fields while
materializing a used height.

## Normal versus explicit stretch control

A non-replaced item with `width:2px;aspect-ratio:1/1` and `align-self:normal`
keeps its derived `[0, 0, 2, 2]` size.

The equivalent item with `align-self:stretch` becomes `[4, 0, 2, 4]` because
its authored block size is still automatic.

A Grid container with omitted `align-items` keeps an aspect-ratio-derived item
at `[0, 0, 2, 2]`; the legacy stored default `stretch` is not mistaken for an
authored explicit stretch declaration.

## Claim boundary

Stretching row or column spans remains outside this single-track slice.

Implicit-row stretch is not claimed.

Flexible and intrinsic track sizing is not claimed.

Replaced-element stretch is not claimed.

The fail-closed replaced classification covers `audio`, `button`, `canvas`,
`embed`, `iframe`, `img`, `input`, `meter`, `object`, `progress`, `select`,
`textarea`, and `video`; the executable boundary control uses `video`.

Auto-margin distribution and center/end positioning are not claimed.

Complete CSS Grid or WPT parity is not claimed.

## Requirements

The executable scenario covers REQ-WEB-BROWSER-003,
REQ-WEB-BROWSER-004, and REQ-WEB-BROWSER-021.

It provides semantic, computed-style, layout, Draw IR, and exact-pixel
evidence for the same authored fixture.

## Evidence status

The SSpec contains direct assertions only.

It contains no placeholder pass, boolean wrapper, or silent evidence branch.

Runtime PASS is reported only from an admitted focused execution.
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.common.ui.draw_ir.{DrawIrCommand}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{
    SimpleWebLayoutDrawIrResult,
    simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result
}
use os.compositor.compositor_engine2d.{Engine2dCompositorBackend}

fn _grid_stretch_rule(selector: text, declarations: text) -> text:
    selector + "{" + declarations + "}"

val GRID_AUTO_STRETCH_HTML = (
    "<style>" + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "html,body", "margin:0;width:8px;height:4px;background:#fff"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#grid", "display:grid;width:8px;grid-template-columns:4px 4px;" +
        "grid-template-rows:4px;gap:0;align-items:stretch"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule("#red", "background:#dc2626") +
    _grid_stretch_rule("#blue", "background:#2563eb") + "</style>" +
    "<main id='grid'><div id='red'></div><div id='blue'></div></main>"
)

val GRID_STRETCH_CONTROLS_HTML = (
    "<style>" + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "html,body", "margin:0;width:20px;height:24px"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#controls", "display:grid;width:20px;" +
        "grid-template-columns:4px 4px 4px 4px 4px;" +
        "grid-template-rows:8px 8px 8px;" +
        "align-items:stretch"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#start", "align-self:start;background:#dc2626"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#auto-margin", "margin-top:auto;background:#16a34a"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#explicit", "height:2px;background:#2563eb"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#boxed", "box-sizing:content-box;margin-top:1px;margin-bottom:1px;" +
        "padding-top:1px;padding-bottom:1px;border-top:1px solid #111827;" +
        "border-bottom:1px solid #111827;background:#f59e0b"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#zero", "height:0px;background:#7c3aed"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#span", "grid-column:1 / span 2;grid-row:2;" +
        "background:#0891b2"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#video", "grid-column:3;grid-row:2;align-self:stretch;" +
        "background:#be123c"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#split-zero", "grid-column:4;grid-row:2;height:0px;" +
        "align-items:stretch;" +
        "background:#4f46e5"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#row-span", "grid-column:5;grid-row:2 / span 2;" +
        "background:#0f766e"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#logical-inline-zero", "grid-column:1;grid-row:3;" +
        "inline-size:0px;background:#9333ea"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#logical-block-zero", "grid-column:2;grid-row:3;" +
        "block-size:0px;background:#ea580c"
    ) + "</style>" +
    "<main id='controls'><div id='start'></div>" +
    "<div id='auto-margin'></div><div id='explicit'></div>" +
    "<div id='boxed'></div><div id='zero'></div>" +
    "<div id='span'></div><video id='video'></video>" +
    "<div id='split-zero' style='visibility:visible'></div>" +
    "<div id='row-span'></div>" +
    "<div id='logical-inline-zero' " +
    "style='writing-mode:vertical-rl'></div>" +
    "<div id='logical-block-zero' " +
    "style='writing-mode:horizontal-tb'></div></main>"
)

val GRID_NESTED_STRETCH_HTML = (
    "<style>" + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "html,body", "margin:0;width:4px;height:4px"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#host", "display:grid;width:4px;grid-template-columns:4px;" +
        "grid-template-rows:4px;align-items:normal"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#nested", "display:grid;grid-template-columns:2px 2px;" +
        "grid-template-rows:4px;align-items:stretch"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule("#left", "background:#dc2626") +
    _grid_stretch_rule("#right", "background:#2563eb") + "</style>" +
    "<main id='host'><div id='nested'>" +
    "<div id='left'></div><div id='right'></div></div></main>"
)

val GRID_ALIGNMENT_MODE_HTML = (
    "<style>" + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "html,body", "margin:0;width:8px;height:4px"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#modes", "display:grid;width:8px;grid-template-columns:4px 4px;" +
        "grid-template-rows:4px;align-items:normal"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#normal-ratio", "width:2px;aspect-ratio:1 / 1;align-self:normal"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#stretch-ratio", "width:2px;aspect-ratio:1 / 1;align-self:stretch"
    ) + "</style>" +
    "<main id='modes'><div id='normal-ratio'></div>" +
    "<div id='stretch-ratio'></div></main>"
)

val GRID_OMITTED_ALIGNMENT_HTML = (
    "<style>" + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "html,body", "margin:0;width:4px;height:4px"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#omitted", "display:grid;width:4px;grid-template-columns:4px;" +
        "grid-template-rows:4px"
    ) + _grid_stretch_rule(
        "#omitted-ratio", "width:2px;aspect-ratio:1 / 1"
    ) + "</style>" +
    "<main id='omitted'><div id='omitted-ratio'></div></main>"
)

fn _grid_stretch_node_index(
    result: SimpleWebLayoutDrawIrResult, component_id: text
) -> i32:
    var index = 0
    for node in result.hit_index.nodes:
        if node.id_attr == component_id:
            return index
        index = index + 1
    fail("missing Grid semantic node: {component_id}")
    -1

fn _grid_stretch_command(
    result: SimpleWebLayoutDrawIrResult, component_id: text
) -> DrawIrCommand:
    for command in result.composition.batches[0].commands:
        if command.component_id == component_id:
            return command
    fail("missing Grid Draw IR command: {component_id}")
    result.composition.batches[0].commands[0]

fn _grid_stretch_style(command: DrawIrCommand, key: text) -> text:
    for property in command.computed_style:
        if property.key == key:
            return property.value
    fail("missing Grid computed style: {key}")
    ""

fn _grid_stretch_box(
    result: SimpleWebLayoutDrawIrResult, component_id: text
) -> [i32]:
    val index = _grid_stretch_node_index(result, component_id)
    val boxes = result.hit_index.boxes
    [boxes.bx[index], boxes.by[index], boxes.bw[index], boxes.bh[index]]

describe "REQ-WEB-BROWSER-003/004/021: CSS Grid auto-size stretch":
    # @manual: show
    # @capture(html)
    # @capture(artifact)
    it "should stretch auto-size items through exact Engine2D pixels":
        # @req: REQ-WEB-BROWSER-003
        step("Parse the styled HTML fixture")
        val result = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            GRID_AUTO_STRETCH_HTML, 8, 4
        )
        val grid_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(result, "grid")
        val red_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(result, "red")
        val blue_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(result, "blue")
        expect(result.hit_index.nodes[grid_index].tag).to_equal("main")
        expect(result.hit_index.nodes[red_index].tag).to_equal("div")
        expect(result.hit_index.nodes[blue_index].tag).to_equal("div")
        expect(result.composition.batches[0].source.source_kind).to_equal(
            "html_ast"
        )

        step("Resolve semantic layout and computed style")
        val grid_style = result.hit_index.styles[grid_index]
        val red_style = result.hit_index.styles[red_index]
        val blue_style = result.hit_index.styles[blue_index]
        expect(grid_style.display).to_equal("grid")
        expect(grid_style.grid_template_columns).to_equal("4px 4px")
        expect(grid_style.grid_template_rows).to_equal("4px")
        expect(grid_style.align_items).to_equal("stretch")
        expect([red_style.height_px, blue_style.height_px]).to_equal([0, 0])
        expect([red_style.height_auto, blue_style.height_auto]).to_equal(
            [true, true]
        )
        expect([red_style.align_self, blue_style.align_self]).to_equal(
            ["auto", "auto"]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(result, "grid")).to_equal([0, 0, 8, 4])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(result, "red")).to_equal([0, 0, 4, 4])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(result, "blue")).to_equal([4, 0, 4, 4])

        val controls = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            GRID_STRETCH_CONTROLS_HTML, 20, 24
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "start")).to_equal([0, 0, 4, 1])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "auto-margin")).to_equal(
            [4, 0, 4, 1]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "explicit")).to_equal(
            [8, 0, 4, 2]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "boxed")).to_equal(
            [12, 1, 4, 6]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "zero")).to_equal([16, 0, 4, 1])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "span")).to_equal([0, 8, 8, 1])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "video")).to_equal([8, 8, 4, 1])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "split-zero")).to_equal(
            [12, 8, 4, 1]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "row-span")).to_equal(
            [16, 8, 4, 1]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "logical-inline-zero")).to_equal(
            [0, 16, 4, 1]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(controls, "logical-block-zero")).to_equal(
            [4, 16, 4, 1]
        )
        val auto_margin_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(
            controls, "auto-margin"
        )
        expect(controls.hit_index.styles[auto_margin_index].margin_t_auto).to_be(
            true
        )
        val zero_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(controls, "zero")
        expect(controls.hit_index.styles[zero_index].height_auto).to_be(false)
        val split_zero_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(
            controls, "split-zero"
        )
        expect(
            controls.hit_index.styles[split_zero_index].height_auto
        ).to_be(false)
        expect(
            controls.hit_index.styles[split_zero_index].align_items
        ).to_equal("stretch")
        expect(
            controls.hit_index.styles[split_zero_index].align_items_authored
        ).to_be(true)
        val logical_inline_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(
            controls, "logical-inline-zero"
        )
        val logical_block_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(
            controls, "logical-block-zero"
        )
        expect([
            controls.hit_index.styles[logical_inline_index].height_px,
            controls.hit_index.styles[logical_block_index].height_px
        ]).to_equal([0, 0])
        expect([
            controls.hit_index.styles[logical_inline_index].height_auto,
            controls.hit_index.styles[logical_block_index].height_auto
        ]).to_equal([false, false])

        val nested = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            GRID_NESTED_STRETCH_HTML, 4, 4
        )
        val nested_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(nested, "nested")
        val host_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(nested, "host")
        expect(nested.hit_index.styles[host_index].align_items).to_equal("normal")
        expect(nested.hit_index.styles[nested_index].display).to_equal("grid")
        expect(nested.hit_index.styles[nested_index].grid_template_columns).to_equal(
            "2px 2px"
        )
        expect(nested.hit_index.styles[nested_index].grid_template_rows).to_equal(
            "4px"
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(nested, "nested")).to_equal([0, 0, 4, 4])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(nested, "left")).to_equal([0, 0, 2, 4])
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(nested, "right")).to_equal([2, 0, 2, 4])

        val modes = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            GRID_ALIGNMENT_MODE_HTML, 8, 4
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(modes, "normal-ratio")).to_equal(
            [0, 0, 2, 2]
        )
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(modes, "stretch-ratio")).to_equal(
            [4, 0, 2, 4]
        )
        val modes_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(modes, "modes")
        expect(modes.hit_index.styles[modes_index].align_items_authored).to_be(
            true
        )

        val omitted = simple_web_layout_render_html_draw_ir_result(
            GRID_OMITTED_ALIGNMENT_HTML, 4, 4
        )
        val omitted_index = _grid_stretch_node_index(omitted, "omitted")
        expect(omitted.hit_index.styles[omitted_index].align_items).to_equal(
            "stretch"
        )
        expect(
            omitted.hit_index.styles[omitted_index].align_items_authored
        ).to_be(false)
        expect(_grid_stretch_box(omitted, "omitted-ratio")).to_equal(
            [0, 0, 2, 2]
        )

        step("Emit canonical Draw IR")
        val grid = _grid_stretch_command(result, "grid")
        val red = _grid_stretch_command(result, "red")
        val blue = _grid_stretch_command(result, "blue")
        expect([grid.kind, red.kind, blue.kind]).to_equal(
            ["rect", "rect", "rect"]
        )
        expect([grid.x, grid.y, grid.width, grid.height]).to_equal(
            [0, 0, 8, 4]
        )
        expect([red.x, red.y, red.width, red.height]).to_equal([0, 0, 4, 4])
        expect([blue.x, blue.y, blue.width, blue.height]).to_equal([4, 0, 4, 4])
        expect([red.color, blue.color]).to_equal(
            [0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFF2563EBu32]
        )
        expect([red.parent_id, blue.parent_id]).to_equal(["grid", "grid"])
        expect([
            grid.clip_rect.x, grid.clip_rect.y,
            grid.clip_rect.width, grid.clip_rect.height
        ]).to_equal([0, 0, 8, 4])
        expect(_grid_stretch_style(grid, "display")).to_equal("grid")
        expect(_grid_stretch_style(grid, "grid-template-rows")).to_equal("4px")
        expect(_grid_stretch_style(grid, "align-items")).to_equal("stretch")

        step("Render exact Engine2D pixels")
        val raster = Engine2dCompositorBackend.create_named(8, 4, "software")
        val rendered = raster.render_draw_ir_composition(result.composition, [])
        raster.shutdown()
        expect(rendered.skipped_command_count).to_equal(0)
        expect(rendered.pixels).to_equal([
            0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32,
            0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32,
            0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32,
            0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32,
            0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32,
            0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32,
            0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32, 0xFFDC2626u32,
            0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32, 0xFF2563EBu32
        ])
